cted":false,"active":false,"prohibit_login":false,"location":"","pronouns":"","website":"","description":"","visibility":"public","followers_count":50,"following_count":2,"starred_repos_count":28,"username":"earl-warren"},"body":"1","created_at":"2023-03-26T23:32:35+02:00","updated_at":"2023-03-26T23:32:35+02:00","old_project_id":0,"project_id":0,"old_milestone":null,"milestone":null,"tracked_time":null,"old_title":"","new_title":"","old_ref":"","new_ref":"","ref_issue":null,"ref_comment":null,"ref_action":"none","ref_commit_sha":"","review_id":0,"label":{"id":83271,"name":"forgejo/privacy","exclusive":false,"is_archived":false,"color":"eb6420","description":"Privacy first","url":"https://codeberg.org/api/v1/repos/forgejo/forgejo/labels/83271"},"assignee":null,"assignee_team":null,"removed_assignee":false,"resolve_doer":null,"dependent_issue":null},{"id":853890,"type":"comment","html_url":"https://codeberg.org/forgejo/forgejo/issues/600#issuecomment-853890","pull_request_url":"","issue_url":"https://codeberg.org/forgejo/forgejo/issues/600","user":{"id":73579,"login":"earl-warren","login_name":"","source_id":0,"full_name":"Earl Warren","email":"earl-warren@noreply.codeberg.org","avatar_url":"https://codeberg.org/avatars/baa02ddebf727ef06a0ded0aee5a25cc","html_url":"https://codeberg.org/earl-warren","language":"","is_admin":false,"last_login":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","created":"2022-11-26T18:56:24+01:00","restricted":false,"active":false,"prohibit_login":false,"location":"","pronouns":"","website":"","description":"","visibility":"public","followers_count":50,"following_count":2,"starred_repos_count":28,"username":"earl-warren"},"body":"It is an interesting border case. Obviously there are pages the user access while logged in that contain information not revealed to the public. Such as the page where they can change their email.\r\n\r\nI would not call that a bug though. Rather an idea to improve privacy?","created_at":"2023-03-26T23:36:51+02:00","updated_at":"2023-03-26T23:36:51+02:00","old_project_id":0,"project_id":0,"old_milestone":null,"milestone":null,"tracked_time":null,"old_title":"","new_title":"","old_ref":"","new_ref":"","ref_issue":null,"ref_comment":null,"ref_action":"none","ref_commit_sha":"","review_id":0,"label":null,"assignee":null,"assignee_team":null,"removed_assignee":false,"resolve_doer":null,"dependent_issue":null},{"id":853895,"type":"comment","html_url":"https://codeberg.org/forgejo/forgejo/issues/600#issuecomment-853895","pull_request_url":"","issue_url":"https://codeberg.org/forgejo/forgejo/issues/600","user":{"id":83403,"login":"SHuRiKeN","login_name":"","source_id":0,"full_name":"","email":"shuriken@noreply.codeberg.org","avatar_url":"https://codeberg.org/avatars/932d6e060857e8952c531cf144d5b539","html_url":"https://codeberg.org/SHuRiKeN","language":"","is_admin":false,"last_login":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","created":"2023-02-08T20:42:04+01:00","restricted":false,"active":false,"prohibit_login":false,"location":"","pronouns":"","website":"https://shuriken.sh","description":"A tinkerer, rustacean 🦀, developing games 🎮, automation 🚀, DeFi \u0026 crypto ₿. Also a fitness enthusiast 💪🏼, following Allah's Guidance ☪︎❤︎","visibility":"public","followers_count":2,"following_count":0,"starred_repos_count":1,"username":"SHuRiKeN"},"body":"\u003e It is an interesting border case. Obviously there are pages the user access while logged in that contain information not revealed to the public. Such as the page where they can change their email.\r\n\u003e \r\n\u003e I would not call that a bug though. Rather an idea to improve privacy?\r\n\r\nYes but User profile should not be one of those pages as that is something people do often.. if someone is showing their own projects or repositories. It is a bug in terms of `should not be the case`. but can be specified as privacy issue sure.","created_at":"2023-03-26T23:39:43+02:00","updated_at":"2023-03-26T23:39:43+02:00","old_project_id":0,"project_id":0,"old_milestone":null,"milestone":null,"tracked_time":null,"old_title":"","new_title":"","old_ref":"","new_ref":"","ref_issue":null,"ref_comment":null,"ref_action":"none","ref_commit_sha":"","review_id":0,"label":null,"assignee":null,"assignee_team":null,"removed_assignee":false,"resolve_doer":null,"dependent_issue":null},{"id":853990,"type":"comment","html_url":"https://codeberg.org/forgejo/forgejo/issues/600#issuecomment-853990","pull_request_url":"","issue_url":"https://codeberg.org/forgejo/forgejo/issues/600","user":{"id":13593,"login":"crystal","login_name":"","source_id":0,"full_name":"crystal","email":"crystal@noreply.codeberg.org","avatar_url":"https://codeberg.org/avatars/f965882a888d78f97338d3df24bcaaedbc903534bc5203e7d451f27ee9176b4a","html_url":"https://codeberg.org/crystal","language":"","is_admin":false,"last_login":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","created":"2020-09-23T05:33:24+02:00","restricted":false,"active":false,"prohibit_login":false,"location":"","pronouns":"she/her","website":"https://hachyderm.io/@crystal","description":"[🔗 nyxal.net](https://www.nyxal.net/)\r\n\u003cbr\u003e\r\n[:forgejo:\u0026nbsp; code.forgejo.org/crystal](https://code.forgejo.org/crystal)","visibility":"public","followers_count":53,"following_count":15,"starred_repos_count":19,"username":"crystal"},"body":"I don't consider this a problem or bug, not really even a privacy issue. It's very common for software to show you some private information which you have access to, but nobody else does. Another good example of this is the public activity tab on your own profile, which is fully functional for you, even if you set it to private. Generally speaking, we don't want to hide private resources from your own profile by default, as that would make it annoying to access your own private repositories.\r\n\r\nOn GitHub, there is a banner across the top of your profile stating that only you can see your full profile, along with a button to show a preview of what anyone else would see. Perhaps we could implement a feature like that. Personally, if I want to preview what my public Forgejo profile looks like, I open a private browsing window and load my profile while logged out.\r\n\r\nIt could be argued that there's no compelling reason to show the email address on your profile if it's set to private anyway. You probably already know what your email address is and you can always check in the user settings panel.","created_at":"2023-03-27T01:50:33+02:00","updated_at":"2023-03-27T01:50:33+02:00","old_project_id":0,"project_id":0,"old_milestone":null,"milestone":null,"tracked_time":null,"old_title":"","new_title":"","old_ref":"","new_ref":"","ref_issue":null,"ref_comment":null,"ref_action":"none","ref_commit_sha":"","review_id":0,"label":null,"assignee":null,"assignee_team":null,"removed_assignee":false,"resolve_doer":null,"dependent_issue":null},{"id":854005,"type":"comment","html_url":"https://codeberg.org/forgejo/forgejo/issues/600#issuecomment-854005","pull_request_url":"","issue_url":"https://codeberg.org/forgejo/forgejo/issues/600","user":{"id":83403,"login":"SHuRiKeN","login_name":"","source_id":0,"full_name":"","email":"shuriken@noreply.codeberg.org","avatar_url":"https://codeberg.org/avatars/932d6e060857e8952c531cf144d5b539","html_url":"https://codeberg.org/SHuRiKeN","language":"","is_admin":false,"last_login":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","created":"2023-02-08T20:42:04+01:00","restricted":false,"active":false,"prohibit_login":false,"location":"","pronouns":"","website":"https://shuriken.sh","description":"A tinkerer, rustacean 🦀, developing games 🎮, automation 🚀, DeFi \u0026 crypto ₿. Also a fitness enthusiast 💪🏼, following Allah's Guidance ☪︎❤︎","visibility":"public","followers_count":2,"following_count":0,"starred_repos_count":1,"username":"SHuRiKeN"},"body":"\u003e I don't consider this a problem or bug, not really even a privacy issue. It's very common for software to show you some private information which you have access to, but nobody else does. Another good example of this is the public activity tab on your own profile, which is fully functional for you, even if you set it to private. Generally speaking, we don't want to hide private resources from your own profile by default, as that would make it annoying to access your own private repositories.\n\u003e \n\u003e On GitHub, there is a banner across the top of your profile stating that only you can see your full profile, along with a button to show a preview of what anyone else would see. Perhaps we could implement a feature like that. Personally, if I want to preview what my public Forgejo profile looks like, I open a private browsing window and load my profile while logged out.\n\u003e \n\u003e It could be argued that there's no compelling reason to show the email address on your profile if it's set to private anyway. You probably already know what your email address is and you can always check in the user settings panel.\n\nThe issue is simply that I can safely open my Github Profile, Gitlab profile and navigate easy to reach locations without exposing my email or any other info.. If I am streaming/recording it is very likely I open my profile up or even link my profile and show etc.. profile is a very very common place to reach out.","created_at":"2023-03-27T02:35:43+02:00","updated_at":"2023-03-27T02:39:54+02:00","old_project_id":0,"project_id":0,"old_milestone":null,"milestone":null,"tracked_time":null,"old_title":"","new_title":"","old_ref":"","new_ref":"","ref_issue":null,"ref_comment":null,"ref_action":"none","ref_commit_sha":"","review_id":0,"label":null,"assignee":null,"assignee_team":null,"removed_assignee":false,"resolve_doer":null,"dependent_issue":null},{"id":854153,"type":"comment","html_url":"https://codeberg.org/forgejo/forgejo/issues/600#issuecomment-854153","pull_request_url":"","issue_url":"https://codeberg.org/forgejo/forgejo/issues/600","user":{"id":-1,"login":"Ghost","login_name":"","source_id":0,"full_name":"","email":"ghost@noreply.codeberg.org","avatar_url":"https://codeberg.org/assets/img/avatar_default.png","html_url":"","language":"","is_admin":false,"last_login":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","created":"1970-01-01T01:00:00+01:00","restricted":false,"active":false,"prohibit_login":false,"location":"","pronouns":"","website":"","description":"","visibility":"public","followers_count":0,"following_count":0,"starred_repos_count":0,"username":"Ghost"},"body":"I do not consider this a bug either. But even though it is arguably a border case, I see why some people would want to have that feature for the purpose described (streaming).\r\n\r\nIt is unlikely to be a priority but if someone is decided to work on it, I can see the appeal.","created_at":"2023-03-27T09:02:22+02:00","updated_at":"2023-03-27T09:02:22+02:00","old_project_id":0,"project_id":0,"old_milestone":null,"milestone":null,"tracked_time":null,"old_title":"","new_title":"","old_ref":"","new_ref":"","ref_issue":null,"ref_comment":null,"ref_action":"none","ref_commit_sha":"","review_id":0,"label":null,"assignee":null,"assignee_team":null,"removed_assignee":false,"resolve_doer":null,"dependent_issue":null},{"id":854154,"type":"change_title","html_url":"https://codeberg.org/forgejo/forgejo/issues/600#issuecomment-854154","pull_request_url":"","issue_url":"https://codeberg.org/forgejo/forgejo/issues/600","user":{"id":-1,"login":"Ghost","login_name":"","source_id":0,"full_name":"","email":"ghost@noreply.codeberg.org","avatar_url":"https://codeberg.org/assets/img/avatar_default.png","html_url":"","language":"","is_admin":false,"last_login":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","created":"1970-01-01T01:00:00+01:00","restricted":false,"active":false,"prohibit_login":false,"location":"","pronouns":"","website":"","description":"","visibility":"public","followers_count":0,"following_count":0,"starred_repos_count":0,"username":"Ghost"},"body":"","created_at":"2023-03-27T09:02:55+02:00","updated_at":"2023-03-27T09:02:55+02:00","old_project_id":0,"project_id":0,"old_milestone":null,"mileston